    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Number 26 is a delightfully bright and spacious four bedroom semi-detached home perfectly positioned in a quiet cul de sac within the well established development of Bellevue Park. The location is exceptionally convenient with a west-facing rear garden, as well as exciting potential for modernisation. \n\nGreystones main street is a few minutes walk away, with an excellent selection of shops, cafés, restaurants and everyday amenities, as well as easy access to local schools. The beautiful coastline and beach are also within easy reach, making this an ideal setting for those looking to enjoy the relaxed coastal lifestyle for which Greystones is renowned.\n\nExcellent transport connections further enhance the location with the nearby Greystones DART station providing a direct rail connection towards Dublin and other destinations, while the N11/M11 road network is easily accessible.\nWhile the property is now in need of modernisation throughout, it offers a wonderful blank canvas for a new owner to create a contemporary home, tailored entirely to their own taste and requirements. The accommodation is well suited to family life, with four good sized bedrooms, kitchen cum breakfast area and two reception rooms providing plenty of flexibility for growing families, guests, home working or additional living space. \n\nProperties in such established and convenient Greystones locations are always highly sought after, and the scope to modernise and enhance this home offers an exciting opportunity to add value while creating a superb family residence.\n\nSPECIAL FEATURES\n\nExcellent location within walking distance of main street, Dart, beaches, shops and schools\nGreat position within quiet cul de sac area\nSuper wide bright and spacious hallway\nGreat potential to upgrade and extend\nLarge windows allow infusions of natural light\nSecond reception room ideal as playroom or office\nDownstairs WC\nWest facing mature rear garden\nGated side entrance\nDriveway provides off street parking\nFully alarmed\n\nACCOMODATION\n\nHallway\nLovely wide welcoming hallway. Bright and airy as there is a full length panelled glass window letting in lots of light. Door leads into:\n\nLivingroom/dining room\nFeature fireplace is clad in natural stone with brass hood, slate hearth and hardwood mantle incorporating imitation/faux coal fire and recessed shelving. The dining area of this room overlooks the delightful garden.\nDownstairs WC\nWhb and wc\n\nOffice/bedroom/playroom\nRecessed lighting. \n\nKitchen cum breakfast room\nFitted high and low level units. Provision for dishwasher, washing machine, oven and fridge freezer. Wood effect lino. Stainless steel sink unit with mixer tap. Door to rear garden.\n\nUPSTAIRS\n\nLanding\nStira access to attic\nShelved hotpress.\n\nBedroom 1\nDouble bedroom overlooking front garden. Extensive range of fitted wardrobes. Tiled step in shower unit\n\nBedroom 2\nDouble bedroom with fitted wardrobes, overlooking front garden\n\nBedroom 3\nOverlooking rear garden with views of Kindlestown Hill. Fitted wardrobes.\nBedroom 4\nOverlooking rear garden with hill views. \n\nBathroom\nTiled walls. Bath with screen. Wc and whb\n\nOUTSIDE\nTo the front :\nTarmac driveway provides off street parking. Selectively planted boundaries with mature hedging to street.\n\nTo the rear: \nWest facing garden mainly laid out in lawn. Gravelled seating area. Purpose built shed. Specimen trees and plants. Timber and walled boundaries. Lovely west facing orientation. Gated side access. "
      },
